WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
So he can call them whatever he wants,

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.360
because that's the freedom of speech.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.360
He can even discourage.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.040
He's threatened to imprison reporters.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:06.960
He wants to imprison.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.120
He said reporters should go to prison for reporting.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.120
He threatened some of them with prison rape.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.240
That is against the First Amendment.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.360
OK, how is that against the First Amendment?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.400
You don't think sending reporters

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.080
to prison for reporting that he doesn't like?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:18.120
Is he sending them?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.639
Did he do that?

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:19.120
He wanted to.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:19.520
He said so.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:20.520
I would like them to go.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.760
I would really like to fight.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.920
So other people stopped him.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.559
Doesn't mean he's not defying the Constitution.

00:00:24.559 --> 00:00:29.040
He also said if you turn up, he can want to do something.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.840
That doesn't mean he will or he can.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.639
And I think he's very aware of that.

00:00:31.639 --> 00:00:32.520
Well, I've already given an example of something

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.320
he did do to the Associated Press, but OK.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.799
Yeah, OK, so the Associated Press

00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:38.119
is allowed in the Oval Office, which is his office.

00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:40.160
That's his executive space.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.840
And they are allowed in the press room, just like CNN,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.360
just like The Guardian.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.560
Which he thinks are illegal media organizations.

